=""&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="18" valign="bottom" style="padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.25pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; width: 3.2316%"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="104" valign="bottom" style="padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.25pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; width: 18.6715%" class=""&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="18" valign="bottom" style="padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.25pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; width: 3.2316%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="108" valign="bottom" style="padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.25pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; width: 19.3896%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="18" valign="bottom" style="padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.25pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; width: 3.2316%"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;  &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/table&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: unset"&gt;(1) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;Represents transportation services purchased from Southern Natural Gas Company (&amp;quot;Southern&amp;quot;), a subsidiary of Kinder Morgan. Florida Gas is currently contracted for firm capacity of up to 100,000 million cubic feet per day on Southern's system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt; (2) Corporate charges and services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt; (3) Compressor equipment parts and related services provided by SEC Energy Products &amp;amp; Services, L.P., an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Accounts receivable from associated companies primarily relate to various administrative and operating costs billed to affiliates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Accounts payable to associated companies primarily relate to transportation services purchased from Southern, current Federal income taxes payable pursuant to a tax sharing agreement with Citrus and various operating and administrative services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas paid cash distributions to Citrus of $559.6 million and $354.9 million during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas received capital contributions of $5.0 million and $12.6 million during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE D - DEBT OBLIGATIONS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0.1pt 0.0001pt 0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: normal; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;The following table sets forth the debt obligations of Florida Gas at the dates indicated:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0.1pt 0 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; cursor: auto"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="697" height="251" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, Florida Gas has scheduled current and long-term debt principal payments, excluding unamortized debt discount and issuance costs,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="656" height="106" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Based on the estimated borrowing rates currently available to Florida Gas for loans with similar terms and average maturities, the aggregate fair value of Florida Gas' debt obligations was $1.8 billion and $1.4 billion as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas recorded interest expense of $64.2 million and $50.5 million net of amounts capitalized of $0.8 million and $0.9 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Senior Notes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;In June 2025, Florida Gas issued $800 million aggregate principal amount of 5.75% senior notes due July 2035.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas used the net proceeds from the offering to repay its $500 million 4.35% senior notes due July 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;In addition, Florida Gas used a portion of the net proceeds to cash settle $80.2 million accounts payable to Citrus and to make a $220.8 million cash distribution to Citrus which Citrus used to repay its $300 million Term loan credit agreement due July 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Covenants Related to Credit Agreements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Under the terms of its debt agreements, Florida Gas may incur additional debt to refinance maturing obligations if the refinancing does not increase aggregate indebtedness, and thereafter, if Citrus' and Florida Gas' debt does not exceed specific debt to total capitalization ratios, as defined in certain debt instruments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Incurrence of additional indebtedness to refinance the current maturities would not result in a debt to capitalization ratio exceeding these limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The agreements relating to Citrus' and Florida Gas' debt include, among other things, restrictions as to the sales of assets and payment of dividends as well as maintenance of certain restrictive financial covenants, including a maximum allowable ratio of funded debt to total capitalization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas is subject, under the currently most restrictive debt covenant of a maximum 65% of funded debt to total capitalization, to a limitation of $752.3 million of total additional indebtedness at December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas guarantees Citrus' revolving credit agreement indebtedness; however, Florida Gas' assets are not pledged as collateral for any of Citrus' debt which also includes a construction and term loan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;All of the debt obligations of Citrus and Florida Gas have events of default that contain commonly used cross-default provisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;An event of default by either Citrus or Florida Gas on any of their borrowed money obligations, in excess of certain thresholds which is not cured within defined grace periods, would cause the other debt obligations of Citrus and Florida Gas to be accelerated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, Florida Gas is in compliance with its debt covenants. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 -0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-indent: 4.5pt"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE E - RETIREMENT BENEFITS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0.1pt 0 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0.1pt 0 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 9pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Other Postretirement Benefit Plans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Postretirement benefits expense for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 reflected the impact of changes Florida Gas adopted as of September 30, 2013 to modify its retiree medical benefits program effective January 1, 2014.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The modification placed all retirees on a common medical benefit platform.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Effective January 1, 2013, participation in the plan was frozen and medical benefits were no longer offered to employees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Obligations and Funded Status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Other postretirement benefit liabilities are accrued on an actuarial basis during the years an employee provides services. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following tables contain information at the dates indicated about the obligations and funded status of Florida Gas' other postretirement plans.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="749" height="512" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Components of Net Periodic Benefit Cost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following tables set forth the components of net periodic benefit cost of Florida Gas' other postretirement benefit plan for the periods presented:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 22.5pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-indent: -0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; cursor: auto"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="714" height="257" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;Assumptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;The weighted average discount rate used in determining benefit obligations was 4.72% and 4.86% at December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;The weighted average assumptions used in determining net periodic benefit cost for the periods presented are shown in the table below:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="601" height="132" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas employs a building block approach in determining the expected long-term rate of return on the plan's assets with proper consideration for diversification and rebalancing. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Historical markets are studied and long-term historical relationships between equities and fixed-income are preserved consistent with the widely accepted capital market principle that assets with higher volatility generate a greater return over the long run. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Current market factors such as inflation and interest rates are evaluated before long-term market assumptions are determined. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Peer data and historical returns are reviewed to check for reasonableness and appropriateness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;The assumed health care cost trend weighted average rates used to measure the expected cost of benefits covered by the plans are shown in the following table:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; position: relative; top: -2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; cursor: auto"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="741" height="178" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; cursor: auto"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Changes in the health care cost trend rate assumptions are not expected to have a significant impact on postretirement benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Plan Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The fair value of Florida Gas' other postretirement plan assets at the dates indicated by asset category is as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; cursor: auto"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="629" height="204" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;span style="text-align: justify; background-color: unset; font-size: 12pt"&gt; (1) Primarily comprised of approximately 71% equity securities and 29% debt securities as of December 31, 2025, and 69% equity securities and 31% debt securities as of December 31, 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-align: justify; background-color: unset; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-align: justify; background-color: unset"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-align: justify; background-color: unset"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Contributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Pursuant to the terms of the Florida Gas rate proceeding, Florida Gas does not expect to contribute to its other postretirement benefit plan in 2026 and will make no contributions annually thereafter, until modified by future rate case proceedings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Benefit Payments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas' estimate of expected benefit payments, which reflect expected future service, as appropriate, in each of the next five years and in the aggregate for the five years thereafter are shown in the following table.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="360" height="239" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The Medicare Prescription Drug Act provides for a prescription drug benefit under Medicare (&amp;quot;Medicare Part D&amp;quot;) as well as a federal subsidy to sponsors of retiree health plans that provide a prescription drug benefit that is at least actuarially equivalent to Medicare Part D. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas does not expect to receive any Medicare Part D subsidies in any future periods.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 -0.1in; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;NOTE F - INCOME TAXES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0.1pt 0 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;The following table provides a summary of the current and deferred components of income tax expense (benefit):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="668" height="323" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The differences between Florida Gas' effective income tax rate and the United States federal income tax statutory rate were as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="688" height="241" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The difference between Florida Gas' effective tax rate and its United States federal income tax statutory rate is primarily attributed to its amortization of a deferred tax benefit offset by state income taxes. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;More specifically, Florida Gas' amortization of a deferred tax benefit due to the 2018 United States federal income tax rate change which decreased its effective tax rate, while state income taxes, net of federal income tax benefit increased its effective tax rate for tax years 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Citrus files a consolidated federal income tax return separate from those of its member. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas is included in the consolidated federal income tax return filed by Citrus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Pursuant to a tax sharing agreement with Citrus, Florida Gas will pay its share of taxes based on its taxable income, which will generally equal the liability that Florida Gas would have incurred as a separate taxpayer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0.1pt 0.0001pt 0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: normal; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Deferred income taxes result from temporary differences between the financial statement carrying amounts and the tax basis of existing assets and liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: normal; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: normal; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;The table below summarizes the principal components of Florida Gas' deferred tax assets (liabilities) at the dates indicated:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0.1pt 0 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: normal; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="687" height="299" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Effective January 1, 2018, Florida Gas began amortizing a regulatory liability resulting from the change in the United States federal income tax statutory rate from 35% to 21% utilizing the Reverse South Georgia Method which resulted in a $19.8 million deferred tax benefit per year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Florida Gas' last rate proceeding as approved on June 3, 2022 adjusted the regulatory liability at June 30, 2021 which resulted in the annual amortization changing from $19.8 million to $17.3 million deferred tax benefit beginning August 1, 2021. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Florida Gas' regulatory liabilities related to the tax rate change had the balance of $345.5 million and $362.8 million in Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;The deferred tax liability for AFUDC - Equity Tax Gross-Up is offset by a regulatory asset which is being amortized over the life of the related plant.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Florida Gas' regulatory assets had the balance of $125.3 million and $126.5 million in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3, respectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 -0.1in; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;NOTE G - UTILITY PLANT:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 -0.1in; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 -0.1in; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;The following table provides a summary of utility plant at the dates indicated:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="767" height="231" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt; &lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; cursor: auto"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.2in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Pursuant to Article VII, Section 1 of the Stipulation and Agreement of Settlement in Docket No. RP21-441-000 et al, the levelization adjustment regulatory asset has a balance of $38.6 million and $62.9 million in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3, as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively, which is being amortized over six years beginning August 1, 2021.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left" style="margin: 0 0 0 0.2in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0.1pt 0.0001pt -0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0.1pt 0.0001pt -0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0.1pt 0.0001pt -0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;NOTE H - ASSET RETIREMENT OBLIGATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas' recorded AROs are primarily related to owned offshore lines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;At the end of the useful life of these underlying assets, Florida Gas is legally or contractually required to abandon in place or remove the asset.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;An ARO is required to be recorded when a legal obligation to retire an asset exists and such obligation can be reasonably estimated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Although a number of other assets in Florida Gas' system are subject to agreements or regulations that give rise to an ARO upon Florida Gas' discontinued use of these assets, AROs were not recorded because these assets have an indeterminate removal or abandonment date given the expected continued use of the assets with proper maintenance or replacement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Individual component assets have been and will continue to be replaced, but the pipeline system is expected to continue in operation as long as supply and demand for natural gas exists.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Based on the widespread use of natural gas in industrial and power generation activities, management expects supply and demand to exist for the foreseeable future. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas has in place a rigorous repair and maintenance program that keeps the pipeline system in good working order.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Therefore, although some of the individual assets on the pipeline system may be replaced, the pipeline system itself will remain intact indefinitely.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table is a general description of the ARO asset recorded in long-lived assets at December 31, 2025:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; cursor: auto"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="716" height="137" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Florida Gas had $3.6 million and $3.4 million, respectively, in legally restricted funds reflected in Other special funds, Account 128, for the purpose of settling AROs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table is a reconciliation of the carrying amount of the ARO liability reflected as liabilities recorded in Asset retirement obligations, Account 230, on the balance sheet for the periods presented.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Changes in assumptions regarding the timing, amount, and probabilities associated with the expected cash flows, as well as the difference in actual versus estimated costs, will result in a change in the amount of the liability recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/gif;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="649" height="206" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1579px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; cursor: auto"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 -0.1in; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;NOTE I -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt; REGULATORY MATTERS, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;COMMITMENTS, CONTINGENCIES AND ENVIRONMENTAL LIABILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;FERC Proceedings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On February 1, 2021, Florida Gas filed a general Natural Gas Act Section 4 rate case pursuant to a 2015 settlement agreement with its shippers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On March 3, 2021, the FERC issued an order accepting and suspending the rates to be effective August 1, 2021, subject to refund, conditions and hearing procedures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;After extensive discovery and settlement negotiations, Florida Gas filed on January 18, 2022, an Offer of Settlement (&amp;quot;Settlement&amp;quot;) to resolve or provide procedures for the resolution of all issues in the case.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The Settlement was approved by FERC's order dated June 3, 2022, with rates to be effective August 1, 2022.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Refunds for the period August 1, 2021 through December 31, 2021 were paid on April 1, 2022.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Refunds for the period January 1, 2022 through July 31, 2022 were paid in September 2022.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The refund report was accepted by the FERC on October 21, 2022.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Also, on May 16, 2022, Florida Gas filed a Partial Settlement to resolve natural gas matters in this docket.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On February 27, 2023, Florida Gas filed a motion with the FERC to withdraw the Partial Settlement and made a tariff filing to propose updates to its tariff for renewable natural gas quality provisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On March 29, 2023, the FERC issued an order accepting and suspending tariff records to be effective August 27, 2023, subject to refund, and the outcome of a technical conference and hearing. The technical conference was convened at the FERC on May 23, 2023. Comments and Reply Comments on the technical conference were filed with the FERC. On August 25, 2023, the FERC issued an order following technical conference, Docket No. RP23-466-000, rejected Florida Gas' proposed tariff records and terminated the proceeding. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On September 25, 2023, Florida Gas filed for rehearing of the FERC's order issued on August 25, 2023.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On January 30, 2024, the FERC sustained the order issued on August 25, 2023, and denied rehearing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On July 10, 2024, Florida Gas filed a Stipulation and Agreement to resolve issues related to renewable natural gas, which was approved by the FERC's order, Docket No. RP23-466-002, issued on December 19, 2024. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Requests for rehearing have been filed with the FERC and the FERC issued an order on rehearing on July 10, 2025 rejecting arguments and reaching the same conclusion as the original order.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;A tariff filing, which was made to implement the settlement on December 30, 2024 and approved by the FERC's order, Docket No. RP23-466-003, issued on January 22, 2025, was effective January 1, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Leases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas utilizes assets under operating leases in several areas of operation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Rental expenses for these leases, including expenses allocated from associated companies, amounted to $4.8 million and $5.0 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Future minimum rental payments of rights-of-way cost are approximately $1.8 million for each of the years ending December, 31, 2026 and 2027, $1.9 million for 2028, $2.0 million for 2029, $2.1 million for 2030, and approximately $69.1 million in aggregate thereafter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Litigation Regarding Jeanerette Lumber &amp;amp; Shingle Co., L.L.C.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On September 27, 2018, Jeanerette Lumber &amp;amp; Shingle Co., L.L.C. (&amp;quot;Plaintiff&amp;quot;) filed suit against Florida Gas, ExxonMobil Oil Corporation, Chevron U.S.A. Inc., and Chevron U.S.A. Holdings, Inc. (collectively, &amp;quot;Defendants&amp;quot;) seeking to hold Defendants liable for compensatory damages and attorneys' fees and costs arising out of the Defendants' pipeline operations on Plaintiff's property located in Louisiana's Atchafalaya Basin.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;In 1963, Plaintiff's predecessor-in-interest granted Florida Gas and others a pipeline rights-of-way over land Plaintiff now owns (the &amp;quot;Rights-of-Way Agreement&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;According to Plaintiff, the Rights-of-Way Agreement imposed certain obligations on Florida Gas, such as maintaining the width of the pipeline canal to 40 feet and arranging the spoil along the canal banks, so it does not impede drainage across the property. Plaintiff contends that the failure to comply with these provisions has affected hydrology and harmed the ecologically valuable cypress-tupelo swampland on Plaintiff's and nearby properties. Plaintiff seeks $18 million in restoration damages for the Florida Gas canal.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas contests Plaintiff's interpretation of the Rights-of-Way Agreement and contends that it has upheld its rights-of-ways in good condition and maintenance in compliance with all state regulatory requirements. Florida Gas further contends it does not owe any damages to Plaintiff, because Plaintiff has not shown causation between its rights-of-way maintenance and any ecological damage.The trial took place on June 2, 2025, in St. Martin Parish, Louisiana.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;After Plaintiff presented its case to the jury, the judge granted Florida Gas' Motion for a Directed Verdict, ending the trial because the Plaintiff failed to prove its case.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Plaintiff filed a motion for the trial judge to recuse himself, alleging that the trial judge did not disclose that one of his new law clerks was a distant cousin of a Florida Gas' trial attorney.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;A magistrate judge appointed by the appellate court heard and denied the motion, but Florida Gas filed an appeal up to the Third Circuit Court of Appeals. The motion is pending oral argument.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Plaintiff also filed a Motion for New Trial, which Florida Gas had opposed as procedurally improper and unnecessary.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;On November 7, 2025, the district court held a hearing on the Plaintiff's motion for new trial, which the trial court denied.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;Plaintiff intends to appeal. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 9pt; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Liabilities for Litigation and Other Claims.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas records accrued liabilities for litigation and other claim costs when management believes a loss is probable and reasonably estimable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;When management believes there is at least a reasonable possibility that a material loss or an additional material loss may have been incurred, Florida Gas discloses (i) an estimate of the possible loss or range of loss in excess of the amount accrued; or (ii) a statement that such an estimate cannot be made.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Florida Gas recorded litigation and other claim-related accrued liabilities of $0.3 million and $0.2 million in Other deferred credits, Account 253, respectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Currently, Florida Gas is not able to estimate the possible losses or range of possible losses in excess of amounts accrued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Except for the matters discussed above, Florida Gas does not have any material litigation or other claim contingency matters assessed as probable or reasonably possible that would require disclosure in the financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.1in"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental Matters. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas' operations are subject to extensive federal, state and local environmental and safety laws and regulations that require expenditures to ensure compliance, including related to air emissions and wastewater discharges, at operating facilities and for remediation at current and former facilities as well as waste disposal sites.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Historically, Florida Gas' environmental compliance costs have not had a material adverse effect on its results of operations but there can be no assurance that such costs will not be material in the future or that such future compliance with existing, amended or new legal requirements will not have a material adverse effect on Florida Gas' business and operating results.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Costs of planning, designing, constructing and operating pipelines and other facilities must incorporate compliance with environmental laws and regulations and safety standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Failure to comply with these laws and regulations may result in the assessment of administrative, civil and criminal penalties, the imposition of investigatory, remedial and corrective action obligations, natural resource damages, the issuance of injunctions in affected areas and the filing of federally authorized citizen suits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Contingent losses related to all significant known environmental matters have been accrued and/or separately disclosed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;However, Florida Gas may revise accrual amounts prior to resolution of a particular contingency based on changes in facts and circumstances or changes in the expected outcome.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental exposures and liabilities are difficult to assess and estimate due to unknown factors such as the magnitude of possible contamination, the timing and extent of remediation, the determination of Florida Gas' liability in proportion to other parties, improvements in cleanup technologies and the extent to which environmental laws and regulations may change in the future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Although environmental costs may have a significant impact on Florida Gas' results of operations for any single period, Florida Gas believes that such costs will not have a material adverse effect on its financial position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.1in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.1in"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Air Quality Standards. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;In 2023, the United States Environmental Protection Agency (&amp;quot;EPA&amp;quot;) finalized its Good Neighbor Plan (the &amp;quot;Plan&amp;quot;) which seeks to reduce nitrogen oxide pollution from power plants and other industrial facilities from 23 upwind states which the EPA determined is contributing to National Ambient Air Quality Standards (&amp;quot;NAAQS&amp;quot;) nonattainment and interfering with maintenance of the 2015 ozone NAAQS in downwind states.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As part of the Plan, the EPA announced that it would be issuing prescriptive emission standards for several sectors, including certain new and existing internal combustion engines of a certain size used in pipeline transportation of natural gas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The EPA's final rule was to become effective on August 4, 2023, and the prescribed emission standards were scheduled to be effective in 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;However, on March 12, 2025, the EPA announced plans to end the Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Operators and industry groups have challenged the Plan in the District of Columbia Circuit (&amp;quot;D.C. Circuit&amp;quot;), as well as the legal predicates to the individual upwind states' inclusion in the Plan in the regional circuits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The effectiveness of the rule is currently stayed in certain states, by nature of judicial stays of the legal predicate to the Plan, by judicial stay of the Plan itself by the United States Supreme Court (&amp;quot;U.S. Supreme Court&amp;quot;), or by the administrative stay issued by the EPA in October 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On June 18, 2025, the U.S. Supreme Court ruled that the regional circuits are the appropriate venue for the proceedings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On July 30, 2025, the United States Court of Appeals for the Tenth Circuit placed the case in abeyance pending the EPA's reconsideration of its disapproval of upwind states' state implementation plans addressing their Plan obligations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Proceedings challenging the Plan in the D.C. Circuit were also placed in abeyance on May 2, 2025 pending the EPA's reconsideration of the Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The EPA is preparing a proposed rulemaking as part of the reconsideration process and on January 27, 2026, the EPA announced its proposal to approve state implementation plans for certain states, which would resolve those states' obligations under the Good Neighbor Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas cannot predict with any certainty the substance of any later proposed rule or the potential impacts on Florida Gas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas currently estimates that the existing final rule would require retrofitting or replacement of certain of its engines used in its operations. Compliance with the Plan (if implementation is not stayed or otherwise delayed) may require substantial capital expenditures which could adversely affect Florida Gas' business in future periods.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;However, at this time, Florida Gas is still assessing the potential costs of this rule and, given uncertainties resulting from the multiple legal challenges filed against the Plan in various states, in the D.C. Circuit and the U.S. Supreme Court, Florida Gas cannot predict with any certainty what the final costs of compliance for the Plan for Florida Gas ultimately may be.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Other Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Federal Pipeline Integrity Rules.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas' pipeline operations are subject to regulation by the United States Department of Transportation under the Pipeline Hazardous Material Safety Administration (&amp;quot;PHMSA&amp;quot;), pursuant to which PHMSA has established requirements relating to the design, installation, testing, construction, operation, replacement and management of pipeline facilities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Moreover, PHMSA, through the Office of Pipeline Safety, has promulgated a rule requiring pipeline operators to develop integrity management programs to comprehensively evaluate their pipelines, and take measures to protect pipeline segments located in what the rule refers to as &amp;quot;high consequence areas&amp;quot; (&amp;quot;HCAs&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Activities under these integrity management programs involve the performance of internal pipeline inspections, pressure testing or other effective means to assess the integrity of these regulated pipeline segments, and the regulations require prompt action to address integrity issues raised by the assessment and analysis. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Integrity testing and assessment of all of these assets will continue, and the results of such testing and assessment could cause Florida Gas to incur future capital and operating expenditures for repairs or upgrades deemed necessary to ensure the continued safe and reliable operation of Florida Gas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas incurred pipeline integrity costs of $57.8 million and $55.7 million for the twelve months ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Florida Gas' operations are also subject to the requirements of the Federal Occupational Safety and Health Act (&amp;quot;OSHA&amp;quot;), and comparable state laws that regulate the protection of the health and safety of employees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;In addition, the Occupational Safety and Health Administration's hazardous communication standard requires that information be maintained about hazardous materials used or produced in Florida Gas' operations and that this information be provided to employees, state and local government authorities and citizens.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Florida Gas believes that its past costs for OSHA required activities, including general industry standards, record keeping requirements and monitoring of occupational exposure to regulated substances have not had a material adverse effect on Florida Gas' results of operations; however, there is no assurance that such costs will not be material in the future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 -0.1in; font-weight: bold; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt;NOTE J -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt"&gt; REVENUE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Contract Balances with Customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Florida Gas satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;The timing of performance may differ from the timing the associated consideration is paid to or received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract asset or a contract liability. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;As of January 1, 2024, the opening balance of accounts receivable from contracts with customers was $72.5 million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Florida Gas recognizes a contract asset when making upfront consideration payments to certain customers or when providing services to customers prior to the time at which Florida Gas is contractually allowed to bill for such services. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, no contract assets have been recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Florida Gas recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes Florida Gas' fulfillment of the performance obligations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, no contract liabilities have been recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Performance Obligation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;At contract inception, Florida Gas assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service (or bundle of goods or services) that is distinct. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;To identify the performance obligations, Florida Gas considers all the goods or services promised in the contract, whether explicitly stated or implied based on customary business practices. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;For a contract that has more than one performance obligation, Florida Gas allocates the total contract consideration it expects to be entitled to, to each distinct performance obligation based on a standalone-selling price basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Certain of Florida Gas' contracts contain variable components, which, when combined with the fixed component, are considered a single performance obligation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;For these types of contracts, only the fixed component of the contracts is included in the amount of revenue expected to be recognized on contracts with customers existing as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, the aggregate amounts of transaction price allocated to unsatisfied (or partially satisfied) performance obligations are approximately $2.6 billion from 2026 through 2028 and $5.6 billion thereafter that Florida Gas expects to recognize as revenue.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.1in; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Practical Expedients Utilized by Florida Gas. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Florida Gas elected the following practical expedients in accordance with ASC Topic 606:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul style="margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0.55in; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Right to invoice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; - Florida Gas elected to utilize an output method to recognize revenue that is based on the amount to which Florida Gas has a right to invoice a customer for services performed to date, if that amount corresponds directly with the value provided to the customer for the related performance or its obligation completed to date. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As such, Florida Gas recognized revenue in the amount to which it had the right to invoice customers. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul style="margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0.55in; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Significant financing component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; - Florida Gas elected not to adjust the promised amount of consideration for the effects of significant financing component if Florida Gas expects, at contract inception, that the period between the transfer of a promised good or service to a customer and when the customer pays for that good or service will be one year or less. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul style="margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0.55in; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Unearned variable consideration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; - Florida Gas elected to only disclose the unearned fixed consideration associated with unsatisfied performance obligations related to Florida Gas' various customer contracts which contain both fixed and variable components.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
    <ferc:AttestationDate id="f-4225" contextRef="c-52">2026-04-14</ferc:AttestationDate>
    <ferc:CorporateOfficerCertificationSignature id="f-4226" contextRef="c-52">/s/  A. Troy Sturrock</ferc:CorporateOfficerCertificationSignature>
