ial, Helvetica, sans-serif">$</span></span><span>        </span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">1,045,814 </span></span></td></tr></table></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1762_47163_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 336 Line No.: 10 Column: b</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt">General Plant is depreciated on a straight line basis per assigned FERC rates.</span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1766_47178_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 338 Line No.: 8 Column: c</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">The applied depreciation rates for General Plant facilities range from 2.5% to 33% pursuant to Article VI of the Stipulation and Agreement of Settlement in Docket No. RP21-441-000, as approved by FERC's o</span><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">rder issued on June 3, 2022.</span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1767_47176_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 338 Line No.: 6 Column: c</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt">The applied depreciation rate for the Transmission Plant Offshore is 1.97% with negative salvage of 0.38% pursuant to Article VI of the Stipulation and Agreement of Settlement in Docket No. RP21-441-000, as approved by FERC's order issued on June 3, 2022.</span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1768_47177_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 338 Line No.: 7 Column: c</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt">The applied depreciation rate for Transmission Plant Onshore is 1.97% with negative salvage of 0.38%.</span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt">The depreciation rate is 1.65% with negative salvage of 0.15% for Phase VIII Expansion Project Onshore transmission facilities.</span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt">These depreciation rates are pursuant to Article VI of the Stipulation and Agreement of Settlement in Docket No. RP21-441-000, as approved by FERC's order issued on June 3, 2022.</span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1771_47175_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 338 Line No.: 6 Column: b</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt">The depreciation plant basis reflects a balance as of 12/31/2025.<span> </span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt">This footnote also applies to lines 7, 8 and 9, column (b).</span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1773_47179_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 338 Line No.: 9 Column: c</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">The applied depreciation rates for intangible assets range from 10% to 33% pursuant to Article VI of the Stipulation and Agreement of Settlement in Docket No. RP21-441-000, as approved by FERC's order issued on June 3, 2022.</span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-2125_47200_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal" class="pasteContent_RTE"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 313 Line No.: 1 Column: c</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal" class="pasteContent_RTE"><span style="font-size: 12pt">The volumes in column (c) include discounted reservation contract quantities and commodity transactions.</span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-2126_47201_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b>Schedule Page: 313 Line No.: 1 Column: e</b></span></p><p style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt">The volumes in column (e) include negotiated reservation contract quantities and commodity transactions.</span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-2317_47395_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold">Schedule Page: 508 Line No.: 30 Column: a</b></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium"><span style="font-size: 12pt">Facility and operation costs are fully reimbursed by customers pursuant to the agreement between Florida Gas Transmission Company, LLC and Florida Power &amp; Light Company. </span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-2381_47376_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold">Schedule Page: 508 Line No.: 31 Column: a</b></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium"><span style="font-size: 12pt">Jointly owned by Florida Gas Transmission Company, LLC (91.75%) and Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Company, LLC (8.25%). Operated by Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Company, LLC. </span></p></div></link:footnote>
